.TH CONTENTS-FSCK 1M "October 2026" "contents-fsck 1.0" "Amix System Administration"
.SH NAME
contents-fsck \- check and repair the installed-software database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B contents-fsck
.I file
.br
.B contents-fsck \-r
[
.B \-s
] [
.B \-b
] [
.B \-o
.I out
]
.I file
.br
.B contents-fsck \-V
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B contents-fsck
checks a
.BR contents (5)
database, normally
.BR /var/sadm/install/contents ,
the record of every file installed packages own.  The Amix 2.1 factory
database ships with records the stock package tools cannot read (a file
named
.B "TrueType Fonts"
with a space in its name, and a duplicated package field); one such record
makes
.BR pkgrm (1M)
and
.B pkginfo \-l
abort.
.PP
Without
.BR \-r ,
.B contents-fsck
only reports.  It prints the number of records of each file type and each
finding with its line number:
.TP 16
.B [unparseable]
no reading of the record is valid; the reason is given
.TP
.B [spaced-path]
a path name that holds a space, recovered by trying each split
.TP
.B [dup-pkg]
a package name repeated at the end of the record
.TP
.B [sort-order]
a path name out of sorted order
.TP
.B [eq-hazard]
a
.B =
in the path name of a record that is not a link; the stock tools split
such a record at the
.B =
.TP
.B [long-line]
a line over 4096 bytes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
Repair: write the repaired database to
.IB file .fixed
(through a temporary file and a rename).  The input is never changed.
Repeated package names are removed, the white space between fields becomes
one space, and comment lines, the record order and records it cannot parse
are kept as they are.
.TP
.B \-s
With
.BR \-r :
drop records with a space in the path name, and print those path names so
the files can be renamed first.  Use it on a system that only has the stock
tools; by default such records are kept.
.TP
.B \-b
With
.BR \-r :
copy the input to
.IB file .bak
first.
.TP
.BI \-o " out"
With
.BR \-r :
write the result to
.I out
instead of
.IB file .fixed\fR.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP 4
.B 0
the database is clean
.TP
.B 1
findings were reported
.TP
.B 2
a usage or I/O error
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# contents-fsck /var/sadm/install/contents
# contents-fsck \-r \-b /var/sadm/install/contents
# cp /var/sadm/install/contents.fixed /var/sadm/install/contents
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP 30
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
the installed-software database
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR contents (5),
.BR pkgchk (1M),
.BR amix-sadm-migrate (1M)
